# SDK Pod Packages

The following packages belong to the SDK pod:

- `packages/sdk`
- `packages/cli`
- `packages/rag`
- `packages/logging`
- `packages/error`
- `packages/ai-sdk-provider`
- `packages/inference`
- `packages/registry-server`
- `plugins/opencode` (tag slug: `opencode-plugin`)
- `plugins/openclaw` (tag slug: `openclaw-plugin`)

When any rule or skill references "SDK pod" or "SDK pod packages", these are the packages in scope.

Changelog / release `--package=` values use the **tag slug** (see `scripts/sdk/package-paths.cjs`).

## Agent stack (release cascade subset)

```text
@qvac/sdk
  -> @qvac/cli
    -> @qvac/ai-sdk-provider
      -> @qvac/opencode-plugin
      -> @qvac/openclaw-plugin
```

`@qvac/bare-sdk` stays lockstep with `@qvac/sdk` via `qv-sdk-bare-sdk-sync` (not listed above). Use `/qv-agent-stack-sync` for plan / prepare-cascade / promote.

## Glob Patterns

```yaml
globs:
  - packages/sdk/**
  - packages/cli/**
  - packages/rag/**
  - packages/logging/**
  - packages/error/**
  - packages/ai-sdk-provider/**
  - packages/inference/**
  - packages/registry-server/**
  - plugins/opencode/**
  - plugins/openclaw/**
```

## Skill Naming Convention

SDK pod skills use the `qv-sdk-` prefix (`qv-sdk-pr-create`, `qv-sdk-changelog`, `qv-sdk-backmerge`, `qv-sdk-e2e-create`, `qv-sdk-pr-status`, `qv-sdk-update-models`). Agent-stack orchestration is `qv-agent-stack-sync`.
